#, no-wrap
msgid "Submission Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid "All entries must be submitted by or before **30th June 2025**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artists may submit as many pieces as they'd like. In fact, the more the "
"merrier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
msgid "Artwork may be traditional or digital."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
msgid "Traditional artwork must be digitally scanned, not photographed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artwork must not be AI-generated or contain AI elements (backgrounds, "
"textures, etc...)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
msgid "Artwork must be colourised."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
msgid "Artwork may not depict anything of an NSFW nature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"All artwork must pertain to the theme \"LIFE OF LEARNING\" (see theme "
"guidelines below)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artwork must be submitted to the email address saint.whom@gmail.com with the "
"email subject \"SOLARPUNK ART 2025.\" A brief description of the work would "
"be appreciated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Submitted artwork should be submitted under [Creative Commons BY 4.0](/tags/"
"cc-by-4.0) or [Creative Commons BY-SA 4.0](/tags/cc-by-sa-4.0). Yo can learn "
"more about them [here](https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/"
"cclicenses/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Submitted artwork may be included in a livestream on the main channel and "
"video on the side channel, as well as being published on [Tumblr](https://"
"andrew-ism.tumblr.com/) and on Story Seed Library. By submitting artwork, "
"you consent to your work being shared in this manner with due credit. I "
"reserve the right to decline submissions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artists should include what, if any, credit they would like to have included "
"in the final showcase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2026/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theme Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artwork must depict people engaged in teaching and learning: literature, "
"sciences, arts, trades, sports, crafts, cooking, husbandry, permaculture, "
"social skills, and more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Consider settings within and outside the classroom or lecture hall. How do "
"mentorships and apprenticeships look lke? Does practical learning happen in "
"libraries, makerspaces and hackerspaces?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Imagine how humanity, nature, and technology interact in your setting - and "
"how it's different from today."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Think how different age groups interact in a setting where lifelong learning "
"is the norm, not only in schools!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Explore the role of research, non-exploitative peer review, and science "
"education."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"What does [Citizen Science](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citizen_science) "
"look like, when regular people care for and monitor the ecosystems around "
"them?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Education and learning is not only about your early life. Look at projects "
"like the [University of the Third Age](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"University_of_the_Third_Age) - maybe there are even some in your area?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"To make people more aware of their surroundings, education and learning "
"should happen within the context of local ecosystems. How can we encourage "
"people to get involved in their own hometowns?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Take a look at the [Story Seeds](/seeds/) and see if any of them inspire you!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artwork must reflect some degree of human diversity. People of different "
"racial and cultural backgrounds, genders and sexualities, abilities, ages, "
"etc, should be included. Solarpunk is for the people. All the people."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artwork may depict urban, semi-urban, and rural spaces, including interiors "
"or exteriors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Greenwashing is not solarpunk. Don't just change a single element about our "
"current world, like adding trees or stained glass to unsustainable "
"buildings. Think about subtler and more beautiful consequences of "
"sustainability - like how making technology repairable can make everything "
"more long-lasting and personalised."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Artwork should be a realistic vision of near-future, with no fantasy or far-"
"future elements. We want to explore how humanity can change, not what "
"magical technology can save us."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/andrewisms-art-collab-2025/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Please indicate in your submission what form(s) of education you are "
"reimagining in your work. Try to venture outside the typical."
msgstr ""

