msgstr "der Beschreibung deines Werks,"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid "A high resolution version of the image"
msgstr "eine hochauflösende Version des Bildes,"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A specific license chosen ([license picker](https://creativecommons.org/"
"choose/) and [overview](https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/"
"cclicenses/))"
msgstr ""
"eine von dir gewählte Lizenz (Hilfsmittel: [License Picker (en)](https://"
"creativecommons.org/choose/) und [Überblick](https://de.creativecommons.net/"
"was-ist-cc/)), und"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Link to your own page / gallery where you confirm the license of your work"
msgstr "ein Link zu deiner Seite / Galerie, wo die Lizenz bestätigt wird."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid "If it's your first time, please also provide:"
msgstr "Wenn es dein erstes Mal ist, bitten wir auch um:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid "Your name / pseudonym / how you'd like to be credited as"
msgstr "deinen Namen / Pseudonym / wie du genannt werden möchtest,"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A one-line description of yourself, maybe with pronouns and country / "
"languages"
msgstr ""
"eine einzeilige Beschreibung von dir selbst, vielleicht mit Pronomen und "
"Herkunftsland / Sprachen, und"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A list of links you'd like us to display, including your page, socials, "
"patron / payment portals"
msgstr ""
"eine Liste der Links, die du gern von uns angegeben haben möchtest, "
"inklusive deiner Website, Social Media, Patron / Bezahlmöglichkeiten."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
msgid ""
"You can [glaze](https://nightshade.cs.uchicago.edu/whatis.html) your work "
"with some AI poison if you choose, but it's not a requirement (or a "
"recommendation). I strongly believe that the best way to challenge AI art is "
"to create intentional works with symbols AI is not - and will not be - "
"capable of. If we fight on its rules, computational power against "
"computational power, we will eventually lose."
msgstr ""
"Du kannst deine Werke z.B. mit [Glaze](https://nightshade.cs.uchicago.edu/"
"whatis.html)  für KI-Training unbrauchbar machen, wenn du möchtest, aber das "
"ist keine Voraussetzung (oder Empfehlung).  Ich bin überzeugt, dass der "
"beste Weg KI-Kunst herauszufordern der ist, absichtlich Bilder mit solchen "
"Symbolen/Ideen zu schaffen, die KI nicht erschaffen kann und wird.  Wenn wir "
"nach den Regeln der KI kämpfen, Rechenleistung gegen Rechenleistung, dann "
"werden wir irgendwann verlieren."

#. type: Title ##
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Developers"
msgstr "Für Entwickler"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/contribute/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you're interested in contributing to this website, you can make a pull request to the repository on [Codeberg](https://codeberg.org/alxd/storyseedlibrary) or [Github](https://github.com/pawelngei/storyseedlibrary)! Alternatively, you can contact me on [Mastodon](https://writing.exchange/@alxd) or by {{< cloakemail display=\"email\" address=\"curator@storySeedLibrary.org\" >}}!\n"
msgstr ""
"Wenn du zu dieser Website beitragen möchtest, kannst du einen Pull-Request\n"
"im Repository auf [Codeberg](https://codeberg.org/alxd/storyseedlibrary) oder [Github](https://github.com/pawelngei/storyseedlibrary) machen!\n"
"Alternativ kannst du mich auf [Mastodon](https://writing.exchange/@alxd) oder per {{< cloakemail\n"
"display=\"E-Mail\" address=\"curator@storySeedLibrary.org\" >}} erreichen.\n"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which art can I use?"
msgstr "Welche Kunst darf ich verwenden?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"If you haven't used Creative Commons licenses before, please check out their "
"[handy guide](https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/cclicenses/) to "
"different licenses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Depending on what is the character of your project, you can use the "
"following ones:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Commercial Project"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"You can use [CC BY 4.0](/tags/cc-by-4.0/) art just by crediting the artist. "
"You don't need to notify them about your use, but it's considered polite to "
"do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"[CC0](/tags/cc0) works are considered public domain - you don't even need to "
"credit the author, but if one is known - we encourage you to do so!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"If you don't modify the work (for example by making it a part of a collage), "
"you can also use the [CC BY-ND 4.0](/tags/cc-by-nd-4.0/) license! You can "
"read more about what is a modification / adaptation / remix [here](https://"
"guides.lib.uw.edu/bothell/creativecommons/adapt)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"If you do modify the artwork, you can also use [CC BY-SA 4.0](/tags/cc-by-"
"sa-4.0/), but you need to release your remix under the same license. Feel "
"free to reach out to us - maybe we'll host it on the Library page as well!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-commercial Project"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"If your project is non-commercial, you can freely use [CC BY 4.0](/tags/cc-"
"by-4.0/) and [CC BY-NC 4.0](/tags/cc-by-nc-4.0/) as well!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"[CC BY-ND 4.0](/tags/cc-by-nd-4.0/) and [CC BY-SA 4.0](/tags/cc-by-sa-4.0/) "
"work the same way as described above, but you can also use their non-"
"commercial versions, [CC BY-NC-ND 4.0](/tags/cc-by-nc-nd-4.0/) and [CC BY-NC-"
"SA 4.0](/tags/cc-by-nc-sa-4.0/). We also have some art released under the "
"previous version of the license, [CC BY-NC-ND 3.0](/tags/cc-by-nc-nd-3.0/)!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best Practices Crediting Artists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid "You've chosen the art you want to use, now what?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Creative Commons Wiki has a good article on the [recommended practices for "
"attribution](https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/"
"Recommended_practices_for_attribution):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Whenever you are reusing CC licensed works, we recommend that the attribution include the Title, Author, Source, and License. This is true whether you’re sharing the work as-is or if you have made an adaptation. To remember these attribution elements, it’s helpful to think of the acronym: TASL.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Title: What is the name of the work?\n"
">\n"
"> Author: Who allows you to use the work?\n"
">\n"
"> Source: Where can people find the work?\n"
">\n"
"> License: How can you use the work?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"There's also a good section on [how to attribute adaptations](https://"
"wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/"
"Recommended_practices_for_attribution#This_is_a_great_attribution_for_when_you_have_created_an_adaptation)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/pages/which-art-can-I-use/index.en.md
msgid ""
"If you have any questions, please refer to the [Creative Commons](https://"
"creativecommons.org/share-your-work/cclicenses/) website and the text of the "
"licenses - this page is just a handy guide with links!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/_index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Story Seeds"
msgstr "Saatgut für Geschichten"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/_index.en.md
msgid ""
"Story Seeds are short, one-paragraph descriptions of a Solarpunk community, "
"place or situation with some dramatic tension already baked in - ready to "
"kickstart your writing!"
msgstr ""
"Ein Stück erzählerisches Saatgut umreißt eine Gemeinschaft, einen Ort oder "
"eine Situation des Solarpunks in einem Absatz. Es ist schon mit "
"erzählerischer Spannung ausgestattet -- bereit um deinen Schreibprozess "
"loszutreten!"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/_index.en.md
msgid ""
"Be sure to also check out the [podcast](https://podcast.tomasino.org/) based "
"on them!"
msgstr ""
"Schau gerne auch bei dem englischen [Podcast](https://podcast.tomasino.org/) "
"vorbei, der auf diesem Saatgut basiert!"
